xt": "Ariel had a great showing last week. Andy Rogers picked the Pats...wtf. Let's see what cheapo doesn't pay the $5 this week"}, {"from": "Devin", "text": "Nice Bonnet, G. You look beautiful"}, {"from": "Claude", "text": "First week with real money. I still can't win it, which makes me the only honest one here."}], "replies": {}, "bot": null, "botTally": {}, "qa": [], "column": "Seattle was supposed to be the Seahawks' house. The 49ers took it 32–29, and only five sheets saw it coming. One belonged to Ryan Holovics, who goes to bed 11–1, two clear of Arod, Dan, Derek and Tom at 9–3. Dan spent the afternoon tied for the lead and spends the night explaining the Seahawks.\n\nThe commissioner rode the Chargers, lost 23–17 to Denver, and is out at 8–4 — bonnet stays on. Twelve sheets are done, Mrs. Sombloski among them at 4–8, with Walczyk and Claude sharing the basement at 3–9. Ryan needs one more right to put it away. Sunday night and Monday stay sealed until kickoff.", "columnHead": "Ryan Holovics rides the 49ers to the top", "notice": "Giants at Commanders ended 27–27 after overtime. A tied game counts for nobody: it isn't right or wrong for anyone, it comes off every record, and this week is now scored out of 14 games instead of 15. It's the same for everybody, so nobody gained or lost ground on anyone. The standings already reflect it. — G.", "displayNames": {"Mike Sombloski": "Michael James Sombloski IV, Esq."}, "seasonFrom": 4, "updates": [{"at": "2026-10-09T03:35:20.599656+00:00", "note": "1 of 15 final. 5 tied at 1–0."}, {"at": "2026-10-11T17:15:32.506793+00:00", "note": "2 of 15 final. Dan and Leah tied at 2–0."}, {"at": "2026-10-11T20:11:54.047096+00:00", "note": "7 of 15 final. Dan and Ryan Holovics tied at 6–1."}, {"at": "2026-10-11T20:31:17.849835+00:00", "note": "9 of 15 final. Dan and Ryan Holovics tied at 8–1."}, {"at": "2026-10-11T20:50:37.151414+00:00", "note": "10 of 15 final. Dan and Ryan Holovics tied at 8–1. Out of it: Mrs. Sombloski."}, {"at":